reply.analysis:
With the 8 obs views added, every single layout scored above 0: transpose 0.79, y-flip 0.63, identity 0.52, x-flip 0.23. The 8 obs views probably let the net pick whichever orientation matches the mask frame, so these scores don't say which layout is correct. Without the obs views, only some layouts score:
- the y-flip + x-flip pair scored 0.23;
- the identity + transpose pair scored 0;
- set A scored 0.19 and set B scored 0.
So relative to the obs, the action frame is most likely flipped on one axis (y or x), not a transpose or a double flip. Round 1 ruled out LayerNorm as a fix: alone it was within noise of plain set A, and combined with the obs views it scored 0. This round splits the flip pair: y-flip and x-flip each alone, without obs views. The correct one should reach about 0.8-0.9 and the wrong one 0. The other four slots refine the current best, transpose + obs views (0.79), one change each: ent_coef 0.01, 16 minibatches, lr 3e-3, and pooled global context added to every head cell.
